          "text": "karm. if its sense can be conveyed by a Bah. So this way of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "defending the form is not very satisfactory. See, however, our",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "note on तुल्यगन्धिषु Rag. IV. 45. जुगुप्सित—censured, condemned.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "निरुपम०–Avya ; ०रसप्रीत्या v. l. see com.; ( eating it ) with a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "relish the flavour of which is unparalleled. न शङ्कते—has no fear",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "or migiving; does not think that he is doing something censur-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "able or disgusting. परिग्रहफल्गुता—the worthlessness of one's",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "belonging. The fi g. here is अर्थान्तरन्यास—Def. सामान्यं वा विशेषो",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "वा तदन्येन समर्थ्यते । यत्र सोर्थान्तरन्यासः साधर्म्येणेतरेण वा । Where a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "particular proposition is corroborated by a general proposi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "tion or a general proposition is supported by a particular",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "instance either under a resemblance or a contrast, that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "is Artha'ntaranyâsa or corroboration. There is also अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "in the first three lines.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 10. शार्वम्–शर्वस्येदं of S'iva. Bhagîratha, a king of the solar",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "race, wishing to procure the salvation of his 60,000 ancestors that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "had been reduced to ashes by Kapila's curse, propitiated, by his",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "penance, Gangâ, and induced her to come down to the earth.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "The river complied with his request but directed him to find",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "out some one who would bear her force as she would fall down",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "from heaven. Bhagîratha then propitiated S'iva who agreed to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "allow the river to fall on his head. Bhágîrathî, accordingly,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "fell from heaven on S'iva's head, thence descended to the peak",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "of Himalaya, thence to the earth and thence to the nether world",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "where her waters sanctified the offspring of Sagara. The whole",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "story is given in Ràma. I. 35-44. For पशुपति०—some read पतति",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "शिरसः तत्क्षितिधरम् ( his i. e. S'iva's mountain). महीध्र—महीं धरतीति,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "धृ+क ( अ ); a mountain. अधोधः—The Ganges comes down to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "a lower and lower position. स्तोक—low, base. अथवा—or rather,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "what wonder if. विवेकभ्रष्टानाम्—Gangâ, in her arrogance thought",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "that she would bear down even S'iva and enter into the nether",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "world with him; she was punished for this by S'iva. See Râm.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 20,
          "text": "विनिपातः—Mark the double entendre on this word which means",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 21,
          "text": "( i ) great fall, and ( ii ) destruction, ruin. शतमुख—applies to",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
